s10-10-p5 = realized (prose (cons "**A concrete long-only order/ledger program.** Fix a natural-number bound \(B\), an identifier type \(\mathsf{Id}\) with decidable equality, and positive quantities. Let \(p\in\mathbb N\) be filled long position, \(O:\mathsf{FinMap}(\mathsf{Id},\mathbb N_{>0})\) the outstanding buy orders, \(U:\mathsf{FinSet}(\mathsf{Id})\) the identifiers ever allocated, \(L:\mathsf{List}(\mathsf{Id}\times\mathbb N_{>0})\) the accepted-fill ledger, and \(Q\) a FIFO queue of authenticated exchange events. The gateway version \(v\) is another state component. Define" (cons "\[" (cons "R(p,O):=p+\sum_{i\in\operatorname{dom}(O)}O(i),\qquad" (cons "I_B(p,O):=R(p,O)\le B." (cons "\tag{10.T1}" (cons "\]" (cons "This bounds the already filled long position **plus** the maximum additional position represented by admitted outstanding buys. It is not a bound on only open orders. The restricted transition relation is generated by the following operations, with all unmentioned components unchanged:" (cons "\[" (cons "\begin{array}{ll}" (cons "\mathsf{Admit}(i,q):&i\notin U,\ q>0,\ R(p,O)+q\le B" (cons "\Rightarrow O':=O[i\mapsto q],\ U':=U\cup\{i\};\\" (cons "\mathsf{Receive}(m):&Q':=Q\mathbin{+\!+}[m];\\" (cons "\mathsf{Fill}(i,q):&Q=\mathsf{FullFill}(i,q)::Q_0,\ O(i)=q" (cons "\Rightarrow O':=O\setminus\{i\},\ p':=p+q,\\" (cons "&\hspace{12mm}L':=L\mathbin{+\!+}[(i,q)],\ Q':=Q_0;\\" (cons "\mathsf{Cancel}(i):&Q=\mathsf{CancelAck}(i)::Q_0,\ i\in\operatorname{dom}(O)" (cons "\Rightarrow O':=O\setminus\{i\},\ Q':=Q_0;\\" (cons "\mathsf{Stale}(m):&Q=m::Q_0,\ \text{no matching open order}" (cons "\Rightarrow Q':=Q_0." (cons "\end{array}" (cons "\tag{10.T2}" (cons "\]" (cons "An admission also emits the corresponding order request to the external exchange; `Receive` is the input event from its handler. These transitions describe a deliberately restricted full-fill, long-only lifecycle, with no partial fills, no position-reducing sells, and no unmodeled preexisting position. For the claimed relation to actual exchange behavior, the handler must authenticate events, preserve per-order exchange sequencing, and make a terminal cancel acknowledgment exclude unaccounted earlier or later fills. Otherwise dropping a stale fill could make the ledger undercount real position. The handler contract is a premise of that correspondence, not a consequence of the gateway's state invariant." nil)))))))))))))))))))))))) (cons (cite GwState "GwState") (cons (cite gw-R "gw-R") (cons (cite gw-IB "gw-IB") (cons (cite GwMove "GwMove") (cons (cite gw-move "gw-move") (cons (cite gw-allowed "gw-allowed") nil))))))
